# STG's copy of STNH's advisor-voice soundgroups. SHADOWS the vendored
# sound/sth_soundgroups.asset harvested from Star Trek New Horizons (688086068).
#
# STNH's l_vo_borg was written against Stellaris 3.x and covered only 52 of
# the 173 advisor sounds vanilla's l_machine overrides, so most of what a Borg
# player heard was the stock advisor. Rebuilt here: renamed events, every
# variant filled, STNH's four misspellings corrected.
#
# Owned in src/ rather than patched in vendor.yml because the Borg group is
# rebuilt, not amended. l_vo_breen and l_vo_rom are carried through
# byte-identical, so this copy is a superset and not a fork.
#
# Filename and l_vo_borg are STNH's, unprefixed: the file has to match to
# shadow, and STH_advisor_voice_types.txt names the key verbatim. Decision 09.
#
# GENERATED by tools/gen_borg_vo.py against /stellaris/sound/soundgroups.asset.
# Every name emitted below is checked to exist in vanilla first, because an
# unknown name is an assetfactory_audio.cpp:901 record and a silent clip.
#
# COVERAGE: 173 of 173 advisor sounds (STNH shipped 52), from 68 of 75 Borg wavs.
#
# STNH CLIPS DELIBERATELY LEFT UNBOUND -- 4.4 has no slot that means this:
#   advisor_notification_army_recruited_01.wav           4.4 has no army-recruited advisor line.
#   advisor_notification_spaceport_upgraded_01.wav       Lost in the starbase rework; 4.4 has no upgrade line for it.
#   advisor_notification_special_project_available_01.wav 4.4 has only special_project_COMPLETE; binding it would announce the wrong thing.
#   advisor_notification_terraform_station_lost_01.wav   4.4 enumerates station losses by type and has no terraform one.
#   biolog...wav                                         Filename truncated in STNH's release, content unidentified. Not bound until someone listens to it.
#   we_are_the_borg_02.wav                               Spare; advisor_sample_vo has only 4 slots.
#   we_are_the_borg_03.wav                               Spare; advisor_sample_vo has only 4 slots.

########## borg

